# A view's owner that closes it while a cell is typed in it doesn't take the typing away, and
# doesn't leave a view that only looks alive (#269). tests/drive.rs installs a csv-table that
# closes its table whenever the file changes, as the example does when the file is gone.
# While a year is typed, another program writes the file: the table stays, the status line
# and the table's own last line say its extension closed it, and it goes when the typing
# ends. With Enter the status line says the edit was not saved, and tests/drive.rs checks the
# file is as the other program wrote it. With Esc it says who closed the view.
size 140x24
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys /
type eruptions
wait-for ▤ Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
keys enter j
wait-for CSV table · ⏎ to open it in csv-table
keys enter
wait-for Mount St. Helens  1980
keys j l e
wait-for Year: 1883▏
keys ctrl+u
type 1884
wait-for Year: 1884▏
write Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv Volcano (link),Year,VEI,Notes (markdown)\nVesuvius,79,5,\nKrakatoa,1883,6,\nTambora,1816,7,\n
wait-for csv-table wanted to close a view: not while a cell is being edited
wait-for its extension closed this view: what you type is not saved
expect Year: 1884▏
screen
keys enter
wait-for not saved: csv-table had closed this view
wait-for CSV table · ⏎ to open it in csv-table
screen
keys enter
wait-for Tambora           1816
keys j l e
wait-for Year: 1883▏
keys ctrl+u
type 1885
wait-for Year: 1885▏
write Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv Volcano (link),Year,VEI,Notes (markdown)\nVesuvius,79,5,\nKrakatoa,1883,6,\n
wait-for its extension closed this view: what you type is not saved
wait-for csv-table wanted to close a view: not while a cell is being edited
expect Year: 1885▏
keys esc
wait-for csv-table closed the view you were typing in
wait-for CSV table · ⏎ to open it in csv-table
keys q
exits 0
